SUMMARY:"Inimigos do fim!" - Tipton-Tsiganov-Lockwood-Barata Quartet
LOCATION:The Lilypad\, 1353 Cambridge St\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:$15 admission / 6pm doors / 6:30 show / seated / all ages "Inim
 igos do Fim!" will feature Brazilian jazz & samba\, original jazz tunes\, 
 and standards played by a dynamic quartet\, including Mark Tipton (trumpet
 )\, Alexei Tsiganov (piano & vibes)\, John Lockwood (bass)\, and Rafael Ba
 rata (drums). "Inimigos do Fim!" translates from Portuguese as "Enemies of
  the end!\," and conveys a spirit of resilience and a passion for life - o
 f refusing to give up! This spirit is at the core of the Tipton-Tsiganov-L
 ockwood-Barata Quartet's music.\nhttps://www.lilypadinman.com/home/2027/1/
 3/inimigos-do-fim\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/
